# Private Learning Notes

- Put repo-owner-only teaching, lessons, walkthroughs, and guidance in `.private/learning-notes.md`.
- Treat `.private/learning-notes.md` as educational notes only, not as source-of-truth project documentation.
- Avoid duplicating project requirements, setup steps, architecture decisions, or implementation truth in the private notes when that information already belongs in code, the `README`, or shared docs.
- When giving substantial educational guidance during Yum4Less implementation, update `.private/learning-notes.md` instead of scattering the same teaching content across multiple files.
- Keep shared docs and code comments focused on the project itself; keep personalized learning content in the private notes file.
